{"evidence":[{"sentence_id":0,"text":"The Academy Award for Best Supporting Actor (often referred to as the Oscar for Best Supporting Actor) is an award presented annually by the Academy of Motion Picture Arts and Sciences (AMPAS).","title":"Academy Award for Best Supporting Actor"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" It is given in honor of an actor who has delivered an outstanding performance in a supporting role while working within the film industry.","title":"Academy Award for Best Supporting Actor"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"This is a list of winners of the Academy Award of Merit for Performance by an Actor in a Supporting Role, presented annually by the Academy of Motion Picture Arts and Sciences (AMPAS) to an actor who has delivered an outstanding performance while working within the film industry.","title":"List of Best Supporting Actor winners by age"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" More popularly known as the Academy Award (or the Oscar) for Best Supporting Actor, this award was initially presented at the 9th Academy Awards ceremony for 1936 and was most recently presented at the 88th Academy Awards ceremony for 2015.","title":"List of Best Supporting Actor winners by age"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" Throughout the past 80 years, accounting for ties and repeat winners, AMPAS has presented a total of 81 Best Supporting Actor awards to 73 different actors.","title":"List of Best Supporting Actor winners by age"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" This list is current as of the 89th Academy Awards ceremony held on February 26, 2017.","title":"List of Best Supporting Actor winners by age"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"The Dark at the Top of the Stairs is a 1960 American drama film.","title":"The Dark at the Top of the Stairs (film)"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" Academy Award winner Delbert Mann directed the work of Robert Preston and Dorothy McGuire in the production.","title":"The Dark at the Top of the Stairs (film)"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" Shirley Knight garnered an Oscar nomination for Best Supporting Actress, and Lee Kinsolving was nominated for a Golden Globe Award as Best Supporting Actor.","title":"The Dark at the Top of the Stairs (film)"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" Knight was also nominated for two Golden Globes.","title":"The Dark at the Top of the Stairs (film)"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" Mann's direction was nominated for a Directors Guild of America Award for Outstanding Directing in a Feature Film.","title":"The Dark at the Top of the Stairs (film)"},{"sentence_id":5,"text":" It was based on the Tony Award nominated play of the same name by William Inge.","title":"The Dark at the Top of the Stairs (film)"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"The British Independent Film Award for Best Supporting Actor is an annual award given to the Best Supporting Actor in a British film.","title":"BIFA Award for Best Supporting Actor"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" The award was introduced at the 2008 ceremony.","title":"BIFA Award for Best Supporting Actor"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" Previously, there had been a single award given for Best Supporting Actor/Actress starting in 2003.","title":"BIFA Award for Best Supporting Actor"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Eric Marlon Bishop (born December 13, 1967), known professionally by his stage name Jamie Foxx, is an American actor, singer, songwriter, musician, producer, and comedian.","title":"Jamie Foxx"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" He won an Academy Award for Best Actor, BAFTA Award for Best Actor in a Leading Role, and a Golden Globe Award for Best Actor in a Musical or Comedy, for his portrayal of Ray Charles in the 2004 biographical film "Ray".","title":"Jamie Foxx"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" The same year, he was nominated for the Academy Award for Best Supporting Actor for his role in the crime film "Collateral".","title":"Jamie Foxx"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" As of spring 2017, Foxx serves as host and executive producer of the new Fox game show "Beat Shazam".","title":"Jamie Foxx"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Akim Mikhailovich Tamiroff (Armenian: Ակիմ Թամիրով , Russian: Аким Михайлович Тамиров ; birth name` Hovakim, Armenian: Հովակիմ ; 29 October 1899 – 17 September 1972) was an ethnic Armenian actor.","title":"Akim Tamiroff"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" He won the first Golden Globe Award for Best Supporting Actor, was nominated twice for the Academy Award for Best Supporting Actor, and appeared in at least 80 American motion pictures in a career spanning thirty-seven years.","title":"Akim Tamiroff"}],"peer_messages":["\".","title":"Jamie Foxx"}
